        "explanation": "Senators Mikulski and Cardin announce federal funding for firefighters, with Senator Mikulski explicitly stating her role on the Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee that funds the program and her ongoing efforts to increase federal funding. This demonstrates credit-claiming by linking the funding to her personal advocacy and committee work."
      },
      {
        "document_id": "4585",
        "explanation": "Senator Schumer announces federal fire grants for Westchester County, explicitly stating that he pushed for additional funding and secured the grants. This is a direct claim of credit for his role in advocating for and obtaining the funds."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator discusses general policy positions, criticizes others, or provides commentary without explicitly or implicitly linking a positive outcome to their personal actions. Statements that focus on the need for action, general support for an issue, or criticism of others without claiming personal responsibility do not qualify as credit-claiming.",
